WEBVTT

00:00:00.792 --> 00:00:05.726
A worker is a machine that stays on and runs your agents:

00:00:05.726 --> 00:00:09.621
a Linux server, or a Mac mini under the desk.

00:00:09.621 --> 00:00:14.036
This is devbox, a fresh Linux server in my tailnet.

00:00:14.036 --> 00:00:15.421
Let's set it up.

00:00:15.794 --> 00:00:17.981
First, install FlightDeck.

00:00:17.981 --> 00:00:21.934
One command downloads it into your home folder.

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:23.364
It needs no root.

00:00:25.661 --> 00:00:29.098
As it says, load the new path into this shell.

00:00:29.517 --> 00:00:36.608
Now one command starts the worker, and hands it to systemd, so it comes back by itself after a reboot.

00:00:36.608 --> 00:00:41.684
If your account needs lingering for that, it tells you how to turn it on.

00:00:42.226 --> 00:00:45.740
The worker offers every agent FlightDeck supports.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:50.168
This box has only Claude Code set up, so switch the others off.

00:00:57.005 --> 00:01:00.442
Let's check that. Reboot the server.

00:01:02.158 --> 00:01:07.034
Once it's back up, log in again, and ask the worker how it's doing.

00:01:09.338 --> 00:01:11.960
It's running, started at boot.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:13.796
Nobody had to log in.

00:01:16.007 --> 00:01:18.947
The worker is ready. Last step:

00:01:18.947 --> 00:01:24.734
pair FlightDeck Desktop with it, with flightdeck worker pair.

00:01:24.734 --> 00:01:27.106
The next video shows how.
